{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel journeyed from Be'erot.</b> That is to say, do not say that at the beginning of the forty years, in the matter of the calf, Aharon died and my prayer did not avail him — for at the end of the forty he died, at Mount HaHor, at that time when the children of Israel journeyed from Be'erot B'nei Ya'akan, when they came there from Moserah, as it is written in the portion of Masei: ״ויסעו ממסורות ויחנו בבני יעקן״ (and they journeyed from Moserot and camped at B'nei Ya'akan), and they went from there to Mount HaHor; there Aharon died — and not in the matter of the calf. <b>There Aharon died.</b> Aharon died then, like ״משם רועה אבן ישראל״ (from there the Shepherd of the Rock of Israel), which means 'from then.' Another interpretation: it is found in the midrash — since his grave was at the top of the mountain, they could see his grave throughout all eight stages of their return journey, until they came to Moserah and it disappeared from them; and they renewed there a great grief over mourning him, and it seemed to them that he had died there. This is what is written: <b>there Aharon died.</b> And this matter too caused them to turn back."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The Hebrew משם רועה אבן ישראל is from Genesis 49:24; Chizkuni reads משם in that verse as 'from then,' and draws the parallel to שם מת אהרן read as 'then Aharon died.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:23.863097373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}